# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  HOW TO FILL THIS IN
#  Copy this file to `.env` at the repo root (the copy is gitignored,
#  this template is not). Fill every value below before running anything.
#
#  AZURE_AI_AGENT_ENDPOINT
#    Foundry portal → your project → "…" menu (top-right) →
#    Project properties → copy the `endpoint` URL (ends in /api/projects/<name>).
#
#  AZURE_AI_AGENT_SUBSCRIPTION_ID
#    Azure portal → Subscriptions → copy the ID hosting the Foundry resource.
#
#  AZURE_AI_AGENT_RESOURCE_GROUP_NAME
#    Foundry portal → project → Management center → Resources → resource group.
#
#  AZURE_AI_AGENT_PROJECT_NAME
#    Foundry portal → project name (shown at top-left).
#
#  AZURE_AI_AGENT_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME
#    Foundry portal → Models + endpoints → find your gpt-5.4 deployment row →
#    copy the "Deployment name" column.
#    NOTE: This is the DEPLOYMENT name you chose at deploy time, NOT the
#    underlying model name. Each agent should be configured to use this
#    deployment (Agent settings → Model).
#
#  REGULATIONS_GOV_API_KEY
#    Request at https://open.gsa.gov/api/regulationsgov/ — the key is issued
#    via api.data.gov and is sent as the `X-Api-Key` header.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AZURE_AI_AGENT_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/your-project
AZURE_AI_AGENT_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=your-subscription-id-here
AZURE_AI_AGENT_RESOURCE_GROUP_NAME=your-resource-group-name
AZURE_AI_AGENT_PROJECT_NAME=your-project-name
AZURE_AI_AGENT_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=gpt-5.4
REGULATIONS_GOV_API_KEY=your_regulations_gov_api_key_here
